Maintenance
===========

Read this before assuming any part of the app is finished.


Correctness gaps
----------------

1. Startup wiring is missing in App.js.
   App.js imports loadSettings from services/settingsStore.js and
   setStoredPushToken from services/pushTokenStore.js and calls neither.

   The consequence of the first is real: settingsStore.getSetting reads a
   synchronous in-memory cache, and nothing populates that cache at launch.
   The persisted Quest reminders and Auto check-in toggles are therefore not
   honoured until the user opens ProfileScreen and the store loads as a side
   effect. Both gates, in services/realtime.js and hooks/useGymProximity.js,
   fall back to true.

   Fix: call loadSettings in a startup effect in App.js.

2. Pin initialisation is not wired.
   services/pinStore.js exports ensurePinsInitialized and clearPinned and
   neither has a call site. ensurePinsInitialized exists to run a one-time
   reset of stale device pin state, which was the cause of new accounts
   appearing with exercises already pinned on a device that had been used by
   a previous account. Without the call, that stale state persists.

   Fix: call it in the same startup effect as loadSettings.

3. The Friends leaderboard tab is out of scope but still on screen.
   LeaderboardScreen shows Friends, Faculty and Campus. The friends system
   was removed from scope; there is no friends endpoint and no friend
   relation in the database. The tab should be removed until the feature is
   built, or it advertises something that cannot work.

4. PushGate discards the token.
   The comment in App.js says the registered token is mirrored into the store
   so logout can unregister it, but PushGate returns null without capturing
   what usePushNotifications gives back. Unregistration on logout depends on
   the token being in the store. Verify this path end to end before trusting
   it.


