Traps
-----

* Provider order in App.js. PushGate must be inside AuthProvider, AppProvider
  must be inside AuthProvider. Reordering breaks token attachment silently.

* Socket listeners must go through services/realtime.js. The socket is created
  after AppContext mounts, so binding directly at mount time attaches to null
  and never fires. This has been diagnosed as a hot-reload bug more than once
  and it is not one.

* Keyboard handling for sheets uses a Keyboard listener that translates the
  sheet by the keyboard height. KeyboardAvoidingView with padding does not
  lift a bottom-pinned sheet. It has been tried and reverted.

* PressScale applies style to an inner animated view. Flex belongs on
  wrapStyle, on the outer pressable. A row that will not spread evenly is
  almost always this.

* Horizontal padding belongs to one element per screen. A padded header inside
  an already padded ScrollView doubles the inset. Every screen puts its header
  outside the scroll view for this reason.

* Page titles are left aligned with a gold edge bar. Centred titles with
  horizontal padding produced a long-running complaint about a gap before the
  title. The offending pattern lived in ChallengeResultSheet.js, not
  ChallengeSheet.js, which cost three passes to find.

* Metro resolves require() at bundle time. Every path in avatarSources.js and
  facultyBadgeSources.js must point at a file that exists, and a change there
  needs npx expo start -c.

* Never flatten facultyKey, level or flagCode when mapping an API response
  into a board row. Hardcoding them makes every student render identically,
  which has shipped once already.

* Charts must use range-aware axis labels. A single shared format truncates:
  three letter months for a year range, day of month for a month range, hour
  only for a day range.

* Batched loads use Promise.allSettled, not Promise.all. HomeStatsWidget once
  blanked every pinned tile because one failing stat request rejected the
  whole batch.


Deferred by scope decision
--------------------------

Recorded so a future team knows these were choices, not oversights.

	Friends system      following, friend-only boards, motivational nudges.
	                    Removed from scope: friend groups, per-group board
	                    scoping, search and activity feeds are a project of
	                    their own. The Friends tab in LeaderboardScreen is
	                    the last trace and should be removed.

	University SSO      students would sign in with their UWindsor account,
	                    validated against university records. Blocked on
	                    UWindsor IT Services approval, whose cycle is longer
	                    than this project. JWT is the authentication layer
	                    for the MVP and was built so SSO can sit in front of
	                    it without reworking the app.


